{"chunk_id": "a49e6a0556e6", "text": "The Creature recounts the moment his hope for human companionship collapses and transforms into vengeance. After the De Lacey family flees in terror, he wanders the forest in a frenzy of rage and despair, ultimately burning their cottage and severing his last emotional tie to humanity. Resolving to confront Victor, he begins a lonely, brutal journey toward Geneva, traveling by night through cold landscapes. A brief return of kindness\u2014saving a drowning girl\u2014ends when he is shot by her guardian, convincing him that humanity will always answer benevolence with violence. Near Geneva he encounters a child, William Frankenstein; realizing the boy belongs to his creator\u2019s family, he kills him and frames Justine by planting a portrait on her. The Creature ends by demanding Victor create a companion like himself.\nAfter the De Laceys flee, the Creature burns their cottage, travels to Geneva, is shot while rescuing a girl, murders William, frames Justine, and demands a female companion.\nThemes: rejection and vengeance, injustice of appearance, creator responsibility, isolation, corruption of innocence", "vector": [0.0025477830786257982, -0.0029849866405129433, -0.010191132314503193, -0.001315040048211813, -0.015074096620082855, 0.024277662858366966, -0.005037272348999977, -0.0017625308828428388, -0.02297462522983551, -0.017721321433782578, 0.010828934609889984, 0.0389539897441864, 0.0024963472969830036, -0.009279005229473114, 0.022508274763822556, 0.013750484213232994, 0.047704920172691345, -0.010012821294367313, 0.02935265377163887, -0.02054685913026333, -0.002762098563835025, 0.030093329027295113, -0.00029982742853462696, -0.01492321863770485, -0.004865819588303566, -0.004965262021869421, 0.009272146970033646, -0.03138265013694763, 0.032562244683504105, -0.008291439153254032, -0.006666070315986872, 0.003399901557713747, 0.0019236961379647255, -0.016349703073501587, -0.028529683127999306, 0.01438828743994236, -0.003867966